<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, analysts said.</p>
<p>The Fed's absence in the market was in line with expectations.</p>
<p>At 1045 EST/1545 GMT, the end of 15 minute period in which the Fed is expected to intervene in the market, federal funds rate traded at 5-1/8 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676 ))</p>
</text>
